  "narrative": {
    "intro": "This ranking lists the top small-business government contractors by contract obligations for FY2027 to date. The dataset shows total obligations of $1.9B for the reporting period. CSI AVIATION, INC leads the list with $278M in obligations, followed by SIGNATURE CHOICE III, LLC with $226M and THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC with $169M. Other named contractors in the top ten include PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC at $99.6M, AKIMA INFRASTRUCTURE PROTECTION LLC at $69.6M, and VETERANS DEVELOPMENT CORPORATION, INC. at $67.9M. SOFTRAMS LLC appears with $59.3M, FOUR SEASONS ENVIRONMENTAL INC with $49.4M, CITADEL FEDERAL SOLUTIONS LLC with $41.7M, and CAPE-APTIM JV1, LLC with $40M. The note clarifies that all figures are contract obligations and that current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing. Use this list to see which small businesses have received the largest contract obligations so far in FY2027.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top small-business contractors so far in FY2027?",
        "body": "CSI AVIATION, INC is the top small-business contractor with $278M in obligations. SIGNATURE CHOICE III, LLC and THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC follow with $226M and $169M respectively. The remaining top-ten contractors include PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC at $99.6M and CAPE-APTIM JV1, LLC at $40M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What does the $1.9B total represent?",
        "body": "The $1.9B figure represents total contract obligations for the listed small-business contractors in FY2027 to date. The note clarifies these totals are partial because the fiscal year is not complete."
      }
    ]
  },
